- How would you adapt for non-uniform I/O sizes?
- How would you test for tail-latency regression under burst bursts?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical I/O throttling in the kernel, including how to enforce per-process quotas across devices, handle bursts, and integrate with the block layer without starving others.

## Key Concepts

- Token bucket per process
- Refill cadence and burst handling
- Cross-device fairness (cgroups/weights)
- Enqueue/wake paths in kernel I/O
